WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.420
Hello, I'm Gav.

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:02.640
Welcome to the Slow Mo Guys.

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:05.110
You've joined me in the middle
of a Dallas wrecking yard.

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:06.570
For a long time, we've been a big fan

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:07.500
of these three blokes

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.450
so we're very excited
to be here to promote

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:10.640
season two of The Grand Tour.

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:11.473
Dan's late.

00:00:11.473 --> 00:00:13.550
There he is!

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:14.440
What is that?

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:15.700
Check it out!

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:16.940
What do you think of this?

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:18.620
It's my RV.
You bought an RV?

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:19.710
Yeah.
Why?

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:20.700
Why, you know, I was thinking,

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.510
we shoot in these remote locations.

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:24.030
I want somewhere to chill
out like a home base.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:24.891
Relax, have a shower.
Makes sense.

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.340
Bit of a road trip,
American dream and all that.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:27.430
Absolutely.

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:28.540
Makes sense to me.
Yeah.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:29.620
So you're saying you have a Grand Tour.

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:30.453
Right, yeah, Grand Tour.

00:00:30.453 --> 00:00:32.907
So it'd be a crime not to
do something involving cars

00:00:32.907 --> 00:00:35.000
and what looks good with
slow motion in cars?

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.250
Well, annihilating the hell out of them.

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:37.470
Smash them, yeah.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.350
Any thoughts?

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:40.920
I was thinking, how about
a four-ton wrecking ball

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.950
and a huge crane usually used
to smash up massive buildings?

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:46.680
Yeah, so it should make
a sizable ding in a car.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:49.020
I mean I think it's
slightly overcompensating

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:50.410
but anyway, we've got some old bangers

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:51.243
we're gonna annihilate.

00:00:51.243 --> 00:00:53.730
And how about we test it on a wall first?

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:55.350
You gotta make sure you've
got a good wrecking ball.

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:56.890
Yeah, benchmark, yeah.
I agree.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.650
Miley Cyrus, that's big!

00:00:58.650 --> 00:00:59.920
Yeah, I wasn't messing around.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:02.880
This is 9,000 pounds or
more than four metric tons

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:03.980
of pure heft.

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:05.790
Big old fat crane, swinging it in.

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:06.623
Yeah.

00:01:06.623 --> 00:01:07.456
So we're gonna hit the wall from behind.

00:01:07.456 --> 00:01:08.913
This is actually a real brick wall.

00:01:09.785 --> 00:01:11.960
Solid, got some support on the back.

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.090
Obviously that'll be nothing
against this, though.

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:16.180
This is coming useful as a blast shield.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:17.866
I'm gonna hug this as close as possible.

00:01:17.866 --> 00:01:18.723
Yeah. The second use.

00:01:18.723 --> 00:01:20.304
Triggering.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:28.690
Oh, man!

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:42.933
Acted like it was nothing!

00:01:43.893 --> 00:01:44.730
It just tore through it like a piece

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:45.880
of paper.
Just like Lego?

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:46.713
Yeah.

00:01:46.713 --> 00:01:47.833
All right, so I think we're
ready to put the cars in.

00:01:47.833 --> 00:01:49.490
Yeah, that was a good test.

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:51.040
We're ready.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:53.560
Our victim, a real American car, isn't it?

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:54.630
Victim number one,

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:55.830
honkin' color!

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:57.026
It's like

00:01:57.026 --> 00:01:58.041
what color is this?

00:01:58.041 --> 00:02:00.697
It's like beige-y, tan, vom-y boke.

00:02:00.697 --> 00:02:02.690
Definitely involves vomit somewhere.

00:02:02.690 --> 00:02:03.610
It does.
A hundred percent.

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:06.660
So we're gonna absolutely
rail it just right there.

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:09.580
I think if we hit it low,
it's more likely to shift.

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:11.570
So we'll give it maximum beans

00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:13.038
and get the hell out of the way.

00:02:15.128 --> 00:02:16.318
There it goes!

00:02:20.556 --> 00:02:21.391
Oh yeah.

00:02:21.391 --> 00:02:25.423
Absolutely turn around,
it's coming, it's coming!

00:02:25.423 --> 00:02:26.256
Oh!

00:02:27.341 --> 00:02:29.140
That's a hit.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:30.773
Just swept it right out frame.

00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:35.100
It's like it just got a
broom and went like this.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:36.540
with the car.

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:38.850
Look, it's buckled that tire.

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:40.020
Look at that!

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:40.853
Wait, what?

00:02:40.853 --> 00:02:42.410
Do you see what's happened
is it's hit the rear

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:45.580
of the car, and this tire
has dug into the ground.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:47.090
It pulled the tire off the wheel.

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:48.030
Yeah!
It ripped the tire

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:50.160
off the wheel and it's caused
the back of the car to go out

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:53.360
and this tire obviously didn't
have as much weight over it

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:54.717
so it span it around the back.

00:02:54.717 --> 00:02:56.760
Oh!
Oh, man.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:58.480
See now, here's your problem.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:00.060
How are you gonna get in the car now

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:00.893
because the handle's broken?

00:03:00.893 --> 00:03:02.210
How are you gonna pick up chicks?

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:04.280
I mean, you could drive it, sure.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:06.070
But how are you gonna pick
up girls if you can't get in?

00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:07.037
That is hefty.

00:03:07.037 --> 00:03:07.930
Do you wanna see if the other door opens

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:08.972
and you can get into the driver's seat?

00:03:08.972 --> 00:03:10.830
Yeah.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:12.310
Oh!

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:14.350
It's like slightly
lower than it was before

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:15.623
'cause the wheel's bent.

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:20.691
Any idea how fast you can?

00:03:20.691 --> 00:03:21.740
Look's like you've pranged it.

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:22.573
What happened here?

00:03:22.573 --> 00:03:23.953
Well, funny story.

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:27.010
All right, let's have a
cheeky look at that footage,

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:27.960
shall we?

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:28.793
I'm up for it.

00:03:28.793 --> 00:03:29.790
Oh, you know what, though?

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:31.390
Wrecking ball's absolutely fine.

00:03:34.622 --> 00:03:35.500
Oh, wow.

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:36.540
You see the window go--

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:39.483
It's sort of, tablecloth
whips the window away.

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:42.860
Now, the car's just like,
moving from one place

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:43.693
to the other.

00:03:43.693 --> 00:03:44.630
What's interesting is that even though

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:46.720
the area of impact is, you know, the size

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:47.840
of the front of the wrecking ball,

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:50.500
it drags in so much extra
material so the dent

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:52.480
is like, twice the size of it.

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:53.620
It's dragging door,

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:56.350
and it just bashed the
whole car out of frame.

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:57.880
See you later.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:58.713
Look at that, you see,

00:03:58.713 --> 00:04:02.340
see there, where the roof
now is becoming kinked

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:04.210
and being like, dragged down its crease.

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:06.116
It's flinging off all the paint.

00:04:06.116 --> 00:04:06.949
Look.

00:04:06.949 --> 00:04:07.782
Oh wow, that's so cool.

00:04:07.782 --> 00:04:09.790
The paint's chipping off in those lines.

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:11.110
So there's an element of
difference to this car.

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:12.947
Oh, I see what you did with that one!

00:04:12.947 --> 00:04:15.230
And the fact that there's no door pillar.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:16.540
Oh, interesting.
Yeah.

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:17.570
The last one, we hit down here.

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:20.630
This one, if we raise
the ball, maybe a foot,

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:22.440
we'll get more sort of
crumplage in the top

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:24.300
and less moving of the whole car.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:25.930
So we're gonna completely change the angle

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:27.020
of which you hit in the car,

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:28.300
so maybe just smash
through the top if you can.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:29.160
Yeah.
All right, cool.

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:30.910
It's really, we don't ever really know

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:31.743
what's gonna happen.

00:04:31.743 --> 00:04:32.690
We're learning all the time.

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:34.713
It's an experiment.
It's an experiment.

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:39.004
Do you think he ever
drops the ball on his job?

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:44.826
It's such a delay from this--

00:04:44.826 --> 00:04:47.183
It really is.

00:04:47.183 --> 00:04:48.653
Oh,

00:04:48.653 --> 00:04:49.486
here it comes!

00:04:52.377 --> 00:04:53.294
Oh, yeah!

00:05:08.138 --> 00:05:10.019
Oh, man.

00:05:10.019 --> 00:05:11.450
I thought that might happen
because we're hitting it

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:12.283
from the top.

00:05:12.283 --> 00:05:13.890
I thought if the roof's strong enough,

00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:14.943
it will flip the car.

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:23.848
Just straight in the window.

00:05:23.848 --> 00:05:24.681
That's cool.

00:05:24.681 --> 00:05:25.900
See the way the back glass burst?

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:27.840
Yeah.
That's wicked.

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:29.390
Look how it's like, almost pushing it

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:30.900
into the floor now,

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:32.400
dragging it along.

00:05:33.944 --> 00:05:36.504
Way worse than being T-boned.

00:05:36.504 --> 00:05:37.663
Look at that,

00:05:37.663 --> 00:05:40.490
that glass is now just aerial glitter.

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:42.280
I like how the glass is
pretty much stationary

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:44.410
but the car is actually being shoved aside

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:45.475
faster than the glass is in the floor.

00:05:45.475 --> 00:05:46.410
Yeah.
Oh, look at that

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:48.760
bend in the tires in the back there.

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:49.593
That's some pressure.

00:05:49.593 --> 00:05:51.430
It's so impressive how strong the roof is,

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:53.410
the fact that it held on

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:55.380
and dragged it.

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:58.000
You wouldn't wanna have been in that one.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.670
The mirror didn't even get touched.

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:02.220
It must have missed the
mirror by about an inch.

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:03.560
Oh there are some coins.

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:04.393
What, where?

00:06:04.393 --> 00:06:05.226
Some pennies.

00:06:05.226 --> 00:06:06.320
I need some change, actually.

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:08.180
Ah, you see, there's your problem.

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.013
What?

00:06:09.013 --> 00:06:09.846
It's upside down.

00:06:12.332 --> 00:06:13.610
It's on its side now, though.

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:14.443
It is.

00:06:14.443 --> 00:06:15.276
Hard to move.

00:06:15.276 --> 00:06:16.109
How are we gonna move it?

00:06:16.109 --> 00:06:16.942
Should we?

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:18.823
Wrecking ball?

00:06:18.823 --> 00:06:19.753
Wrecking ball.
Wrecking ball.

00:06:20.857 --> 00:06:22.431
It's like someone just punting it.

00:06:22.431 --> 00:06:23.652
Yeah.

00:06:23.652 --> 00:06:26.289
With a really big shoe.

00:06:26.289 --> 00:06:27.456
There it goes!

00:06:29.992 --> 00:06:30.825
Oh!

00:06:31.919 --> 00:06:33.002
It did a 180!

00:06:36.005 --> 00:06:37.430
Oh!

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:39.070
Flipped it, I thought it was
just gonna go on its roof.

00:06:39.070 --> 00:06:41.600
So it looks like one more
hit and it will be back

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:42.534
on its wheels!

00:06:42.534 --> 00:06:44.050
Goodness sake!

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:46.260
Shockingly sturdy, the
underside of the car, isn't it?

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:47.940
Yeah, I mean, it's just
I think that's where

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:49.680
all the strength is, so,

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:51.230
the fact that it,

00:06:51.230 --> 00:06:53.840
it just brushed off the wrecking ball

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:55.985
and all the force went
into flipping the car.

00:06:55.985 --> 00:06:57.870
Oh!

00:06:57.870 --> 00:06:59.800
Also, I think it's less sturdy on its side

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:02.200
than it is with the wheels on the floor.

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:03.033
So it's more--

00:07:03.033 --> 00:07:04.420
More like, it's no longer bottom-heavy.

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:05.253
Yeah.

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:08.840
So that's some good swinging.

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:10.200
Yeah.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:11.950
How do you feel about dropping?

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:12.900
I like dropping.

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:14.100
Let's do some dropping.

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:16.260
So we've hit the bottom of
one and we've hit the side.

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:17.093
Yeah.

00:07:17.093 --> 00:07:18.480
Well now, we'll just
let gravity do the work

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:19.320
right on the front.

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:20.910
See, the idea is pull it all the way up,

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:23.060
push the emergency release, then drop it.

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:25.150
Basically just dropping the
equivalent of a small elephant

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:26.400
onto the bonnet, so yeah.
Yeah.

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:28.210
Like a female African Elephant.

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:29.080
Yeah.

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:30.010
All right,
very specific.

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:30.843
Let's do it.

00:07:37.904 --> 00:07:38.821
Oh!

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:47.470
That,

00:07:47.470 --> 00:07:48.763
well it just landed in the car.

00:07:48.763 --> 00:07:50.560
It's parked in the car.

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:52.040
It's just parked in it.

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:53.350
You know what?

00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:56.609
That hit the ground so
hard, it shook the camera.

00:07:56.609 --> 00:07:57.720
Look at this, look at this camera shake.

00:07:57.720 --> 00:07:59.114
What, like a giant--

00:07:59.114 --> 00:08:00.260
whoa!

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:02.510
Like a giant's first
step, like in the films

00:08:02.510 --> 00:08:03.350
when like, the dust moves.

00:08:03.350 --> 00:08:04.860
If there was a cup of water on the floor,

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:05.920
it would have been T-Rex'ed--

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:07.883
Like Godzilla-style.

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:11.370
Look at this GoPro, it just sat there.

00:08:11.370 --> 00:08:12.840
We could have killed that GoPro.

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:13.990
It's amazing it's alive.

00:08:13.990 --> 00:08:15.470
9,000 pounds with a GoPro.

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:16.303
We'd do it.

00:08:16.303 --> 00:08:17.136
Oh!

00:08:17.136 --> 00:08:17.969
Look at how the,

00:08:17.969 --> 00:08:19.040
the side window burst.

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:20.560
Oh, on the other side.

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:21.393
Yeah, on the other side.

00:08:21.393 --> 00:08:22.670
It was there one second, the next second

00:08:22.670 --> 00:08:24.502
it just burst.

00:08:24.502 --> 00:08:25.431
It just exploded.

00:08:25.431 --> 00:08:26.264
Excellent.

00:08:26.264 --> 00:08:27.440
That went really deep in the car, there.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:28.590
I'm convinced the wrecking ball

00:08:28.590 --> 00:08:30.170
actually just hit the ground there.

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:31.003
Yeah.

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:35.200
I feel like we should
try and hit it again.

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:36.883
Try and hit it right here.

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:39.313
Thanks for that.

00:08:39.313 --> 00:08:40.320
Sorry, straight onto the bonnet?

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:41.780
Yeah.

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:43.410
I mean, where's the steering wheel?

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:44.243
Uh.

00:08:44.243 --> 00:08:46.110
It's in the seat.
Look at that.

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:50.240
The steering wheel would be in your legs.

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:51.384
Look!

00:08:51.384 --> 00:08:53.530
It just popped out this.

00:08:53.530 --> 00:08:55.976
It's just like

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:58.453
Oh!

00:09:01.070 --> 00:09:03.200
That's the destruction we wanted, right?

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:04.740
Goodness, me!

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:05.870
Unbelievable.

00:09:05.870 --> 00:09:06.970
Where is the engine?

00:09:08.009 --> 00:09:09.797
Do you know when car makers say,

00:09:09.797 --> 00:09:12.030
"Oh, we couldn't fit a bigger engine in?"

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:13.350
Yes, you could.

00:09:13.350 --> 00:09:16.950
I don't think a window's
ever been more smashed.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:19.220
You know, when they say you
take a brick to the window?

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:20.053
Yeah.

00:09:20.053 --> 00:09:22.380
This is about the size
and width of the window.

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:23.980
The middle of it there,
where it actually landed,

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:26.110
it's turned all the glass back to sand.

00:09:26.110 --> 00:09:28.293
Yeah, it's now powder.

00:09:30.174 --> 00:09:32.930
It couldn't have been more
centered on the engine.

00:09:32.930 --> 00:09:33.763
Perfect.

00:09:37.874 --> 00:09:39.760
Whoa, that is destruction.

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:42.000
What you gotta remember is
there's an engine there.

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:44.448
There's like, there's a solid
chunk of metal in the way.

